&io;
// Self method calls: an instance method MUST be invoked through `self.NAME(...)`.
// A bare `NAME(...)` is now resolved as DATA (a local variable / member), never as
// a hidden self-dispatch — so the data/behavior boundary stays clean.
// 自调用：实例方法必须用 `self.NAME(...)` 显式调用。裸写 `NAME(...)` 现在被解析为
// 数据（局部变量 / 成员），而非隐式自派发——数据 / 行为边界因此清晰。
//   - explicit:  self.twice(21)     (`self` keyword = the current instance)
//   - explicit:  self.greet()       (the `self` keyword also reads members)
// Input/output parameters are usable variables you operate on directly:
// `answer << x` publishes x as the output.
// 输入 / 输出参数都是可直接操作的变量：`answer << x` 把 x 公布为输出。
$Program {
    @:: << [() -> () {
        -(io::OStream out);

        out << "self.twice(21) = ";
        out << self.twice(21);

        out << " | self.greet() = ";
        -(std::String g) << self.greet();
        out << g;
    }];

    // Identity method: echoes its input. Demonstrates that the input param
    // `x` and the output param `answer` are ordinary, directly-operable
    // variables (no `=:`/`<<` ceremony needed just to read them).
    // 恒等方法：回显输入。证明输入参数 x 与输出参数 answer 都是可直接操作的
    // 普通变量。
    @twice << [(x[std::Number]) -> (answer[std::Number]) {
        answer << x;
    }];

    @greet << [() -> (msg[std::String]) {
        msg << "hello from self";
    }];
}
